<title>USA: China Pacific seeks South Korean partner.</title>
<headline>China Pacific seeks South Korean partner.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Pacific Inc on Tuesday said it will seek a joint venture partner in South Korea in an effort to increase production capacity and diversify into more product lines.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it believes boosting production and broadening its products should make it more competitive and successful in China's steel markets.</p>
<p>Chief Executive Officer Clement Mak recently visited South Korea and hired a technical advisor to work on the feasibility of upgrading one facility, the company said.</p>
</text>
